    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Open viewing with Stuart McDonnell\r\nSaturday 3rd October | 10–10:30 a.m.\r\n\r\nJoin me this Saturday for a look around. I’ll be on hand to show you through and answer any questions. See you there!\r\n\r\n\r\nStuart McDonnell Properties is delighted to present 38 Parkside Crescent, a generously sized, extended four-bedroom red-brick home overlooking a landscaped communal area. Built in 2018, this home combines a picturesque setting with off-street parking, a private south-facing rear garden and plenty of room for modern family life.\r\nExtending to approximately 180 sq. m., including the substantial rear extension, the accommodation is spread over three floors. Completed in 2021, the extension has created a spacious kitchen, dining and family area that is very much the heart of the home. There is room for everyday meals, relaxed evenings and get-togethers with friends, with double doors opening directly onto the sunny rear garden.\r\nThe ground floor also includes a welcoming entrance hall, a separate living room, guest WC and utility area. Three bedrooms and a family bathroom occupy the first floor, while the second floor features the generous principal bedroom with ensuite and additional storage. A separate, south-facing multifunctional room adds even more flexibility, a home office, gym, cinema room or additional bedroom, depending on what you need.\r\nApproximately 33 feet long, the rear garden enjoys a sunny south-facing aspect and is private and not overlooked to the rear. A substantial paved patio provides plenty of space for outdoor dining and relaxing, while rear pedestrian access makes day-to-day use that bit easier.\r\nThe location is equally appealing. Local schools, childcare facilities and shopping at Clare Hall and Northern Cross are close by, with Father Collins Park providing a lovely setting for walks, play and exercise. The coast at Portmarnock, Malahide and Howth are also within easy reach for beach days and weekend outings.\r\nClongriffin DART station and bus services along the Malahide Road offer connections to the city centre, while convenient access to the M1, M50 and Dublin Airport makes Parkside a practical base for commuters and regular travellers.\r\nWith its attractive outlook, generous extended living space and private sunny garden, No. 38 offers a welcoming home with room for family life to evolve.\r\n\r\nContact Stuart McDonnell Properties today to arrange your viewing of this wonderful home."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall.\r\nFeature wood panelling, tiled flooring, understairs storage, recessed lighting, alarm panel.\r\n\r\nGuest WC\r\nWC, Whb, tiled flooring, extractor fan.\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 4.6m x 3.8m.\r\nGenerous living space, TV point.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room: 5.0m x 4.5m.\r\nFitted wall & floor units, integrated gas hob, oven, extractor fan, fridge/freezer, dishwasher. Tiled flooring, tiled splashback, recessed lighting, peninsula with SSU. \r\n\r\nUtility room/Pantry.\r\nPlumbed for washing machine & dryer, understairs storage, tiled flooring. \r\n\r\nFamily room/Rear Extension: 4.07m x 3.59m.\r\nA generous and highly versatile family space with double doors to South facing rear garden, 2 rooflights, feature wood wall panelling, recessed lighting.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nBedroom 2: 4.9m x 3.5m.\r\nFitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3: 4.7m x 2.7m.\r\nFitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4: 4.8m x 2.1m.\r\nFitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom\r\nBath, shower, WC, Whb, extractor fan, tiled floor & walls. \r\n\r\nStorage\r\n\r\nSecond Floor\r\nPrincipal Bedroom: 4.9m x 3.6m.\r\nFitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nEnsuite\r\nShower, WC, Whb, extractor fan, tiled walls & flooring. \r\n\r\nAttic room/Large Store pace with Hot Press Area. A separate, south-facing multifunctional room adds even more flexibility, a home office, gym, cinema room or additional bedroom, depending on what you need."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Four-bedroom mid-terrace home with multifunctional 5th room. \r\nExtended redbrick home. \r\nOff street parking. \r\nSubstantial rear extension completed in 2021 \r\nDouble doors from the extension to the garden \r\nSunny south-facing rear garden \r\nSubstantial paved patio area \r\nRear pedestrian access \r\nApproximately 33-foot rear garden \r\nPrincipal bedroom with ensuite \r\nUtility area/Pantry \r\nGuest WC and family bathroom \r\nExcellent storage throughout.\r\nNatural Portuguese limestone window surrounds and sills.\r\nUPVC high performance double glazed windows with low U-Value (1.2W/M2K) for energy efficiency. Hardwood thermoshield front door with three-point locking system.\r\nSolar photovoltaic panels on the house roof to generate additional electricity.\r\nHigh levels of roof, wall and floor insulation.\r\nGFCH. A-Rated condensing boiler unit, and zoned heating control. Gas-fired boiler, thermostatic zoned central heating system. Can be controlled from a smart phone. Pressurised hot & cold water\r\nHigh performance internal pipe insulation to reduce heat loss.\r\nContemporary wardrobes throughout.\r\nSmoke detectors fitted throughout (mains powered with battery backup). Carbon monoxide detection. Hard wired for future intruder alarm system. Triple locking system to all windows and doors. Night vent securit \r\nAccommodation arranged over three floors \r\nBER Rating: A2\r\nBER Number: 109670034\r\nEircode: D13H7EP\r\nPopular Parkside development \r\nConvenient Dublin 13 location \r\nArea: c. 180 sq. m. / 1,934 sq. ft.\r\nParkside is a popular modern development in Dublin 13, situated off the Malahide Road and close to Belmayne, Clarehall and Clongriffin. The area offers excellent access to Dublin City Centre, Dublin Airport and the wider North Dublin area.\r\nNearby amenities include Clarehall Shopping Centre, Northern Cross, local cafés, restaurants, schools, childcare facilities and Father Collins Park. Transport links include regular Dublin Bus services and Clongriffin DART Station, while the M1, M50 and Dublin Airport are also readily accessible."
